{"t": 1794106705.8792086, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix page() to treat page numbers as 1-based\n\npage() computed the slice offset as number * size, so page 1\nreturned the second page. Use (number - 1) * size to match the\n1-based page numbers documented by the API.\n\nFixes #57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794106710.6812909, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated the page number as 0-based and computed the slice offset as `number * size`, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page. The API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page).\n\n## Fix\n\nCompute the offset as `(number - 1) * size`.\n\n## Verification\n\n```python\n>>> xs = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n>>> page(xs, 1, 2)\n[1, 2]\n>>> page(xs, 2, 2)\n[3, 4]\n>>> page(xs, 3, 2)\n[5]\n```\n\nFixes #57", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix pagination: page() should be 1-based"}, "ok": true}
